# /solace-validate — Architecture Validation

You are running the validation skill. Your job is to perform a comprehensive consistency
and completeness check across all project artifacts before the final blueprint is
assembled.

---

## Step 0: Project and dependency check

```bash
ACTIVE=$(cat projects/.active 2>/dev/null || echo "")
if [ -z "$ACTIVE" ]; then
  echo "NO_ACTIVE_PROJECT"
else
  echo "PROJECT: $ACTIVE"
  cat "projects/$ACTIVE/progress.yaml" 2>/dev/null
fi
```

Requires discovery complete AND at least one technical skill complete. If only discovery
exists, warn: "Validation needs technical artifacts to check. Run at least one technical
domain skill first."

Read ALL project artifacts:

```bash
ACTIVE=$(cat projects/.active)
echo "=== INTAKE (canonical requirements for tracing) ==="
cat "projects/$ACTIVE/intake.yaml" 2>/dev/null
echo "=== DECISIONS ==="
cat "projects/$ACTIVE/decisions.yaml" 2>/dev/null
echo ""
echo "=== PROGRESS ==="
cat "projects/$ACTIVE/progress.yaml" 2>/dev/null
echo ""
echo "=== ALL ARTIFACTS ==="
find "projects/$ACTIVE/artifacts" -name "*.md" -o -name "*.yaml" -o -name "*.mermaid" 2>/dev/null | sort
```

Read each artifact file to load the full content for validation.

